Does not change your existing RptRbpCost logic
USE [CES]
GO

SET ANSI_NULLS ON
GO

SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON
GO

ALTER PROCEDURE [SBCES].[InternalRbPrice]
AS
BEGIN
    SET NOCOUNT ON;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- DEBUG / CONTROL VARIABLES
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    DECLARE @ProcessedCount INT = 0;
    DECLARE @SkippedCount   INT = 0;
    DECLARE @ErrorCount     INT = 0;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- Clear previous results
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    TRUNCATE TABLE SBCES.TempRbpCost;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- Variables
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    DECLARE @RebuiltStockNum VARCHAR(30);
    DECLARE @MmsStockCode    VARCHAR(30);
    DECLARE @DetailedDesc    VARCHAR(250);

    -- Raw value from StockCodedParts
    DECLARE @RawBuyNewCost   VARCHAR(100);

    -- Cleaned/display value
    DECLARE @BuyNewCost      VARCHAR(30);

    DECLARE @Active           BIT;
    DECLARE @Keyword          VARCHAR(250);

    DECLARE @TotalPrice       DECIMAL(25,10);

    -- Parsed numeric value used ONLY for validation
    DECLARE @BuyNewCostNumeric DECIMAL(25,10);

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- Cursor
    --
    -- IMPORTANT:
    -- Do NOT call ROUND() directly on SCP.MmsNewCost here.
    -- Convert it to VARCHAR first so one bad value cannot kill the cursor.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    DECLARE rb_cursor CURSOR LOCAL FAST_FORWARD FOR
        SELECT
            RBM.RebuiltStockNum,
            SCP.MmsStockCode,
            RBM.DetailedDesc,

            -- Keep original value as VARCHAR.
            -- This prevents SQL Server from performing an implicit
            -- VARCHAR -> NUMERIC conversion in the cursor SELECT.
            CONVERT(VARCHAR(100), SCP.MmsNewCost) AS RawBuyNewCost,

            RBM.Active,
            RBM.Keyword
        FROM SBCES.RbMasterlist RBM
        LEFT JOIN SBCES.StockCodedParts SCP
            ON RBM.MmsStockCode = SCP.MmsStockCode
        ORDER BY RBM.RebuiltStockNum DESC;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- Open cursor
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    OPEN rb_cursor;

    FETCH NEXT FROM rb_cursor
    INTO
        @RebuiltStockNum,
        @MmsStockCode,
        @DetailedDesc,
        @RawBuyNewCost,
        @Active,
        @Keyword;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- Process rows
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    WHILE @@FETCH_STATUS = 0
    BEGIN

        SET @ProcessedCount = @ProcessedCount + 1;

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- Reset variables for current row
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        SET @BuyNewCost = NULL;
        SET @BuyNewCostNumeric = NULL;
        SET @TotalPrice = NULL;

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- DEBUG: Show current row
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        RAISERROR(
            '[InternalRbPrice] Processing #%d | RebuiltStockNum=%s | MmsStockCode=%s | RawMmsNewCost=%s',
            10,
            1,
            @ProcessedCount,
            ISNULL(@RebuiltStockNum, '<NULL>'),
            ISNULL(@MmsStockCode, '<NULL>'),
            ISNULL(@RawBuyNewCost, '<NULL>')
        ) WITH NOWAIT;

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- Convert / validate Buy New Cost
        --
        -- Remove:
        --   $
        --   comma
        --
        -- Then attempt numeric conversion.
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        SET @BuyNewCostNumeric =
            TRY_CONVERT(
                DECIMAL(25,10),
                REPLACE(
                    REPLACE(
                        LTRIM(RTRIM(ISNULL(@RawBuyNewCost, ''))),
                        '$',
                        ''
                    ),
                    ',',
                    '.'
                )
            );

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- BAD DATA
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        IF @RawBuyNewCost IS NOT NULL
           AND LTRIM(RTRIM(@RawBuyNewCost)) <> ''
           AND @BuyNewCostNumeric IS NULL
        BEGIN

            SET @SkippedCount = @SkippedCount + 1;

            RAISERROR(
                '[InternalRbPrice] *** SKIPPED BAD ROW *** | RebuiltStockNum=%s | MmsStockCode=%s | RawMmsNewCost=[%s] | Reason=Cannot convert to numeric',
                10,
                1,
                ISNULL(@RebuiltStockNum, '<NULL>'),
                ISNULL(@MmsStockCode, '<NULL>'),
                ISNULL(@RawBuyNewCost, '<NULL>')
            ) WITH NOWAIT;

            -----------------------------------------------------------------
            -- Skip this row
            -----------------------------------------------------------------
            FETCH NEXT FROM rb_cursor
            INTO
                @RebuiltStockNum,
                @MmsStockCode,
                @DetailedDesc,
                @RawBuyNewCost,
                @Active,
                @Keyword;

            CONTINUE;
        END;

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- NULL cost
        --
        -- Your original SQL converted NULL to '0.00'.
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        IF @RawBuyNewCost IS NULL
           OR LTRIM(RTRIM(@RawBuyNewCost)) = ''
        BEGIN

            SET @BuyNewCost = '0.00';
            SET @BuyNewCostNumeric = 0;

            RAISERROR(
                '[InternalRbPrice] NULL/BLANK cost -> using 0.00 | RebuiltStockNum=%s | MmsStockCode=%s',
                10,
                1,
                ISNULL(@RebuiltStockNum, '<NULL>'),
                ISNULL(@MmsStockCode, '<NULL>')
            ) WITH NOWAIT;
        END
        ELSE
        BEGIN

            -----------------------------------------------------------------
            -- Format the validated numeric value to 2 decimals.
            -----------------------------------------------------------------
            SET @BuyNewCost =
                CONVERT(
                    VARCHAR(30),
                    CAST(ROUND(@BuyNewCostNumeric, 2) AS DECIMAL(25,2))
                );

            -----------------------------------------------------------------
            -- Remove possible leading/trailing spaces
            -----------------------------------------------------------------
            SET @BuyNewCost = LTRIM(RTRIM(@BuyNewCost));

        END;

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- Existing RptRbpCost call
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        /*
        EXEC SBCES.RptRbpCost
            @viRbnum     = UPPER(@RebuiltStockNum),
            @viLinkType  = 'RB',
            @voTotalCost = @TotalPrice OUTPUT;
        */

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- INSERT
        --
        -- Protect INSERT as well. There may be another VARCHAR -> NUMERIC
        -- conversion in TempRbpCost itself.
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        BEGIN TRY

            INSERT INTO SBCES.TempRbpCost
            VALUES
            (
                @RebuiltStockNum,
                @TotalPrice,
                @DetailedDesc,
                @BuyNewCost,
                @Active,
                @Keyword
            );

        END TRY
        BEGIN CATCH

            SET @ErrorCount = @ErrorCount + 1;

            RAISERROR(
                '[InternalRbPrice] *** INSERT ERROR - ROW SKIPPED *** | RebuiltStockNum=%s | MmsStockCode=%s | RawMmsNewCost=[%s] | BuyNewCost=[%s] | Error=%s',
                10,
                1,
                ISNULL(@RebuiltStockNum, '<NULL>'),
                ISNULL(@MmsStockCode, '<NULL>'),
                ISNULL(@RawBuyNewCost, '<NULL>'),
                ISNULL(@BuyNewCost, '<NULL>'),
                ERROR_MESSAGE()
            ) WITH NOWAIT;

        END CATCH;

        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        -- Next row
        ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        FETCH NEXT FROM rb_cursor
        INTO
            @RebuiltStockNum,
            @MmsStockCode,
            @DetailedDesc,
            @RawBuyNewCost,
            @Active,
            @Keyword;

    END;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- Cleanup
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    CLOSE rb_cursor;
    DEALLOCATE rb_cursor;

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    -- FINAL SUMMARY
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    RAISERROR(
        '[InternalRbPrice] COMPLETE | Processed=%d | BadCostSkipped=%d | InsertErrors=%d',
        10,
        1,
        @ProcessedCount,
        @SkippedCount,
        @ErrorCount
    ) WITH NOWAIT;

END;
GO
What you should see

When you run:

EXEC SBCES.InternalRbPrice;

you should get messages similar to:

[InternalRbPrice] Processing #125 | RebuiltStockNum=RB12345 | MmsStockCode=ABC123 | RawMmsNewCost=$125.50

[InternalRbPrice] Processing #126 | RebuiltStockNum=RB12344 | MmsStockCode=ABC124 | RawMmsNewCost=N/A

[InternalRbPrice] *** SKIPPED BAD ROW *** |
RebuiltStockNum=RB12344 |
MmsStockCode=ABC124 |
RawMmsNewCost=[N/A] |
Reason=Cannot convert to numeric

[InternalRbPrice] Processing #127 | RebuiltStockNum=RB12343 | MmsStockCode=ABC125 | RawMmsNewCost=$200.00

[InternalRbPrice] COMPLETE | Processed=127 | BadCostSkipped=1 | InsertErrors=0

That gives you the exact offending row.

One important concern with your original conversion

Your original expression:

REPLACE(REPLACE(ROUND(SCP.MmsNewCost, 2), ',', '.'), '$', '')

has a potential second problem.

If your source contains:

$1,234.56

then blindly replacing comma with . produces:

1.234.56

which is not a valid decimal.

So before deciding the final production conversion, we should determine what SCP.MmsNewCost actually contains.

Run this diagnostic query:

SELECT
    SCP.MmsStockCode,
    SCP.MmsNewCost,
    DATALENGTH(SCP.MmsNewCost) AS DataLength,
    TRY_CONVERT(
        DECIMAL(25,10),
        REPLACE(
            REPLACE(
                LTRIM(RTRIM(CONVERT(VARCHAR(100), SCP.MmsNewCost))),
                '$',
                ''
            ),
            ',',
            '.'
        )
    ) AS ParsedValue
FROM SBCES.StockCodedParts SCP
WHERE SCP.MmsNewCost IS NOT NULL
  AND TRY_CONVERT(
        DECIMAL(25,10),
        REPLACE(
            REPLACE(
                LTRIM(RTRIM(CONVERT(VARCHAR(100), SCP.MmsNewCost))),
                '$',
                ''
            ),
            ',',
            '.'
        )
      ) IS NULL;

This will give you the bad MmsStockCode and actual MmsNewCost values without throwing an error.

Also check the destination table

There is another possibility: the error may not be coming from SCP.MmsNewCost. It could be coming from this:

INSERT INTO SBCES.TempRbpCost
VALUES (...)

For example, if TempRbpCost.BuyNewCost is DECIMAL while your @BuyNewCost is VARCHAR, SQL Server could throw the same Msg 8114.

So I strongly recommend checking:

EXEC sp_help 'SBCES.TempRbpCost';

If you paste the output/schema of SBCES.TempRbpCost and SBCES.StockCodedParts, I can pinpoint whether the 8114 is from the cursor SELECT or the INSERT and give you the final production version without unnecessary conversions.
